1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Last time on Zombieland Saga, we ironed out some of the details about our name and group leader.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,800
We decided Saki should be in charge, and that our group's called Franchuchu.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,000
That really screams cute zombie girls, don't you think?

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Once that was all squared away, we had a gorilla-style pop-up show in the street.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,400
It was our first time doing anything idyllish, and that was cool, but it's pretty clear we have a long way to go.

6
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,200
We'll have to keep practicing till we die all over again.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,400
But I believe in me, and I believe in Franchuchu!

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Good morning, ladies!

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Oh, come on, you look like you're dead inside!

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Good morning!

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Good morning to you too, sir.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Okay, first thing, it looks like you've been taking your lessons pretty seriously lately.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
By the way, how have you been settling into your new name?

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Franchuchu?

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
You're saying it wrong, it's Franchuchu!

16
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Franny Fanny Chuchu!

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Franchuchu!

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Yeah, yeah, I know, it's Flannel Fufu!

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
We have a French name, look how cute we are!

20
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Okay, Franchuchuchu, even though only a month ago at that gorilla concert, you were still just a brain-dead gaggle of drooling zombies,

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
you all may have improved the tiniest bit.

22
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
And this is the part where the real game begins.

23
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Right, boss?

24
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Uh, yeah, I guess.

25
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Spoken like a true leader.

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
What's your take on it, Lily?

27
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Me? I'll do it!

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Great!

29
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Ah!

30
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Now, which one of you ladies would like to guess what your next move should be?

31
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Sakura!

32
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Oh!

33
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
I'm not sure.

34
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Maybe it's time for us to record a single and put it out?

35
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Excellent!

36
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
You've got a good head on your shoulders!

37
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Let me just call up a recording studio and-

38
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
No, dumbass!

39
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Are you crazy?

40
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Where are we gonna get the money?

41
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You honestly think I made a single buck off of you and your raggedy-ass performances so far?

42
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Not to mention your expenses!

43
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Somebody's gotta make sure there's gas in the van, you dumb zombie!

44
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
My point is, our budget's as dry as your skin.

45
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Huh?

46
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
So what's your plan?

47
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The only solution is get more money.

48
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
I'm sorry, what?

49
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Does Saga even have businesses that would hire idols?

50
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Thanks to my supreme awesomeness, yes!

51
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
And it's a big-name pharmaceutical company known as Hisanaka!

52
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
We can form a partnership if this goes well!

53
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Partnership?

54
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
This is way over my head.

55
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Just tell me when it's supposed to go down.

56
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
We start right now.

57
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Now?

58
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
The old group they had booked for their company trip is no longer available.

59
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Your ideas are so last minute.

60
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Cause we can't afford to miss any chances!

61
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Idols have a limited shelf life nowadays, you know?

62
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
And it's not like I can work you girls to death, am I right?

63
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
We're doing it and that's final.

64
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Just don't stop practicing!

65
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
We have to knock their socks off!

66
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Next up, the Urishino Hot Springs.

67
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Hot Springs?

68
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
So we get to take a real bath?

69
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
We've just been hosing off in the yard!

70
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Perhaps this is the perfect opportunity to cleanse a bit of stench and decay from our rancid flesh.

71
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
They're kind enough to let us stay the night, so please behave yourselves.

72
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,000
We get to stay?

73
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
That means plenty of time to chill out!

74
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
There will be no hot springs fun for you!

75
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Cause you won't be able to leave your rooms unless you're in your full makeup!

76
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Sucks to be you!

77
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,000
And besides, if you've got time to splish splash in a hot spring, then you've got time to practice!

78
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Ow!

79
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Sir?

80
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
What's that?

81
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
This pharmaceutical company.

82
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Do they sell pills, or...?

83
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Check it out!

84
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Sagan...ship...sea?

85
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
This pharmaceutical company.

86
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Do they sell pills, or...?

87
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Check it out!

88
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Sagan...ship...sea?

89
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
See?

90
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:22,803
Okay, you're room number 606. You go on at 6 p.m., got it?

91
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,263
Understood, sir.

92
00:05:24,643 --> 00:05:29,463
I went to the trouble of reserving a rehearsal space for you, so you girls better practice while I'm gone.

93
00:05:29,983 --> 00:05:33,823
Of course. Wait, what will you be doing, Mr. Kotaro?

94
00:05:35,483 --> 00:05:35,963
Sightseeing.

95
00:05:38,363 --> 00:05:40,783
The sightseekers see themselves!

96
00:05:40,783 --> 00:05:47,783
Okie dokie, where do we want to go first?

97
00:05:48,303 --> 00:05:49,303
Uh, to the room?

98
00:05:49,343 --> 00:05:52,043
Of all the cool stuff we could do, you really pick work.

99
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,183
We should practice.

100
00:05:53,383 --> 00:05:57,183
Yeah, later. Not while Shades is out painting the town without a care in the world.

101
00:05:57,303 --> 00:05:58,183
No, now.

102
00:05:58,403 --> 00:05:59,963
Look, do you want to die?

103
00:06:00,783 --> 00:06:03,823
Come on, we've been cooped up in the house for a solid month.

104
00:06:04,043 --> 00:06:06,463
Let's take advantage of Urashino while we're here.

105
00:06:06,643 --> 00:06:08,163
I want to go for a walk.

106
00:06:08,263 --> 00:06:09,563
The squirt knows what's up.

107
00:06:09,563 --> 00:06:12,243
I said my name's Lily, not Squirt.

108
00:06:13,363 --> 00:06:15,563
I suppose we can relax for a bit.

109
00:06:16,203 --> 00:06:19,063
I haven't seen a modern-day city yet, and I'd like to explore.

110
00:06:19,483 --> 00:06:21,263
We look totally normal with makeup.

111
00:06:21,603 --> 00:06:24,383
If we're super careful, no one will be able to tell we're zombies.

112
00:06:24,783 --> 00:06:25,963
Good thinking, Squirt.

113
00:06:26,203 --> 00:06:27,223
My name is Lily.

114
00:06:29,743 --> 00:06:31,603
If that's what we all want.

115
00:06:32,723 --> 00:06:34,363
Aye, Junko, what's your vote?

116
00:06:34,363 --> 00:06:40,043
It seems risky, but...

117
00:06:40,043 --> 00:06:56,523
Listen to this, Junko.

118
00:06:56,803 --> 00:06:59,483
That sculpture is said to make you healthier and help your skin.

119
00:06:59,723 --> 00:07:01,223
You have to splash water on it.

120
00:07:01,223 --> 00:07:02,723
Let's do it.

121
00:07:04,903 --> 00:07:06,283
Damn, look at him go.

122
00:07:06,623 --> 00:07:07,143
Crazy.

123
00:07:07,143 --> 00:07:09,023
Uh-huh.

124
00:07:09,023 --> 00:07:29,083
It's such an honor to hear from an esteemed company like Hisanaka Pharmaceuticals.

125
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:32,103
We heard about you from the people who manage the inn.

126
00:07:32,483 --> 00:07:37,883
How fortuitous that my regular interactions with local businesses in the Chamber of Commerce has led us to this encounter.

127
00:07:38,403 --> 00:07:41,543
A Saga-based idol group? That must be hard these days.

128
00:07:41,723 --> 00:07:44,263
It can feel like we're fighting the flow of history.

129
00:07:44,483 --> 00:07:48,403
But the way I see it, if we make even the smallest impact, it's all worth it.

130
00:07:49,423 --> 00:07:50,463
That's wonderful.

131
00:07:51,023 --> 00:07:53,003
We're planning to bring new life to Saga.

132
00:07:53,003 --> 00:07:57,643
As a matter of fact, that idea is at the core of every endeavor Franshushu undertakes.

133
00:07:58,023 --> 00:07:59,323
New life to Saga.

134
00:07:59,783 --> 00:08:00,143
Right.

135
00:08:00,663 --> 00:08:06,783
You and I may be in two different fields, but my group has a great admiration for your company's standing as one of the biggest in the prefecture.

136
00:08:06,983 --> 00:08:12,783
Well, I appreciate the kind words, but we're actually working on ways to expand our overall customer base.

137
00:08:13,043 --> 00:08:15,863
We would like for our brand to appeal to a younger demographic.

138
00:08:16,303 --> 00:08:18,583
In that case, we might just be what you're looking for.

139
00:08:18,583 --> 00:08:22,803
If we were to become partners, I'm confident we could meet and exceed your expectations.

140
00:08:23,203 --> 00:08:26,083
I'm looking forward to this evening's performance, then.

141
00:08:26,383 --> 00:08:27,643
That's excellent to hear.

142
00:08:27,923 --> 00:08:30,583
My hardworking girls are practicing their hearts, so...

143
00:08:31,443 --> 00:08:32,583
Right...

144
00:08:32,583 --> 00:08:33,723
Now.

145
00:08:35,403 --> 00:08:36,883
Is something the matter?

146
00:08:37,403 --> 00:08:37,663
Oh.

147
00:08:41,663 --> 00:08:42,263
Oh.

148
00:08:46,323 --> 00:08:47,323
Oh, wow.

149
00:08:47,323 --> 00:08:48,523
This feels great.

150
00:08:48,763 --> 00:08:50,023
I've never used one before.

151
00:08:50,263 --> 00:08:51,663
Nothing short of heavenly.

152
00:08:52,503 --> 00:08:55,123
It's still a little crazy that this is happening, though.

153
00:08:55,283 --> 00:08:56,303
What do you mean?

154
00:08:56,563 --> 00:09:00,983
Well, if we hadn't come back from the dead, the seven of us would never have gotten the chance to meet each other.

155
00:09:01,303 --> 00:09:03,083
Because we're all from different times, you know?

156
00:09:03,323 --> 00:09:03,863
Oh, yeah.

157
00:09:03,963 --> 00:09:05,763
And the best part is I don't feel dead.

158
00:09:06,083 --> 00:09:07,103
It's not too bad.

159
00:09:07,363 --> 00:09:11,403
Even if we were alive at the same time, I wouldn't have hung out with Saga.

160
00:09:11,523 --> 00:09:12,343
Shut your yap!

161
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:15,903
Well, honestly, you all make me feel like I'm a young girl again.

162
00:09:15,903 --> 00:09:16,903
Oh, yeah, that's right.

163
00:09:17,123 --> 00:09:18,843
It must be so different for you.

164
00:09:19,363 --> 00:09:21,143
But bodies are cremated in Japan.

165
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:23,223
So how'd we get like this?

166
00:09:26,303 --> 00:09:28,803
I'm a little curious about Mr. Tatsumi.

167
00:09:29,763 --> 00:09:30,763
Don't look at me!

168
00:09:30,763 --> 00:09:33,703
Well, you were the first one of us to awaken, right?

169
00:09:34,123 --> 00:09:35,923
Yeah, but I don't know why or how.

170
00:09:36,643 --> 00:09:38,423
Oh, well, just let it go.

171
00:09:38,823 --> 00:09:41,323
Not like you'd give us a straight answer if we asked.

172
00:09:41,703 --> 00:09:46,163
The one thing we do know for sure is that we're here now enjoying this awesome foot bath together.

173
00:09:46,363 --> 00:09:47,463
See? Aren't you glad?

174
00:09:48,143 --> 00:09:49,903
But we really do need to practice.

175
00:09:50,243 --> 00:09:50,823
Yeah, I know.

176
00:09:50,823 --> 00:10:02,623
So, tell me, do you think we have any chance of making it as a real idol group?

177
00:10:03,303 --> 00:10:06,163
That depends. What do you think it means to be real idols?

178
00:10:07,383 --> 00:10:13,663
Uh, like singing and dancing, making people feel happy, and creating lots of excitement.

179
00:10:13,663 --> 00:10:16,943
If that's it, we have a lot more practicing and learning to do.

180
00:10:21,083 --> 00:10:23,823
So if we work harder, do you think we'll pull it off?

181
00:10:23,823 --> 00:10:44,163
Listen, I'll do all that I can.

182
00:10:44,803 --> 00:10:47,283
Everything I said last time, I meant it.

183
00:10:47,283 --> 00:10:54,243
I don't like to half-ass, so count me all the way in.

184
00:10:55,463 --> 00:10:59,743
To the art of performing, I swore my life, and now my death.

185
00:11:00,783 --> 00:11:03,203
Trust me, I know how hard showbiz can be.

186
00:11:04,403 --> 00:11:06,063
As for me...

187
00:11:06,063 --> 00:11:09,203
I always used to do things alone.

188
00:11:09,763 --> 00:11:13,803
That's why the thought of being a team doesn't always sit well with me.

189
00:11:13,803 --> 00:11:22,663
That said, if the rest of you really feel strongly about this, then maybe I'd better do my part too, right?

190
00:11:22,923 --> 00:11:23,843
Thanks, Junko.

191
00:11:24,243 --> 00:11:27,483
But look, the second I feel like this might not work, I'm out.

192
00:11:27,543 --> 00:11:29,383
I swear you won't feel that way.

193
00:11:30,723 --> 00:11:31,623
Oh yeah!

194
00:11:32,203 --> 00:11:34,923
They're not gonna know what hit them when they see our concert later!

195
00:11:35,263 --> 00:11:37,083
Oh, fine! How do we make that happen?

196
00:11:37,503 --> 00:11:38,543
Ah, not sure.

197
00:11:38,543 --> 00:11:43,923
If we do our best to service them, I'm certain the result will be pleasurable for all parties.

198
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:46,263
Wow, we need to work on your phrasing!

199
00:11:46,723 --> 00:11:50,703
We should probably start by finding out everything we can about the product they're selling.

200
00:11:50,883 --> 00:11:53,983
Oh yeah! We don't even know what Sagan Ship Z is supposed to do!

201
00:11:54,343 --> 00:11:56,443
I say we go try it out right now!

202
00:11:56,843 --> 00:11:57,183
Yeah!

203
00:11:57,183 --> 00:12:14,003
So you just slap these suckers on and they make your back and shoulders feel good?

204
00:12:14,123 --> 00:12:15,403
That's the general idea.

205
00:12:15,623 --> 00:12:17,523
For real? That's what's up!

206
00:12:17,703 --> 00:12:21,123
Says you can't put them on other people because it counts as practicing medicine.

207
00:12:21,823 --> 00:12:23,043
Like I give a crap.

208
00:12:23,283 --> 00:12:25,383
And besides, we're not people, we're zombies.

209
00:12:25,383 --> 00:12:28,403
Uh, I don't think there's really a difference.

210
00:12:28,703 --> 00:12:29,103
Hey!

211
00:12:29,463 --> 00:12:29,643
Ha!

212
00:12:30,563 --> 00:12:30,903
Ah!

213
00:12:35,283 --> 00:12:38,263
Awesome! It's like all my muscle fatigue is melting away!

214
00:12:38,363 --> 00:12:39,183
That's so cool!

215
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,923
Guess we absorb stuff faster!

216
00:12:41,183 --> 00:12:41,943
Look at me!

217
00:12:42,123 --> 00:12:44,703
I can move as much as I want and it doesn't fall off!

218
00:12:45,763 --> 00:12:46,163
Ah!

219
00:12:47,063 --> 00:12:48,503
You should try it, Ai!

220
00:12:48,723 --> 00:12:50,203
No, I'd rather not.

221
00:12:50,323 --> 00:12:51,483
I don't have any pain.

222
00:12:51,483 --> 00:12:51,823
Ah!

223
00:12:53,043 --> 00:12:53,483
Ah!

224
00:12:55,383 --> 00:13:02,363
Let's use this in the show somehow.

225
00:13:02,783 --> 00:13:05,123
That way, everyone can see how well it works!

226
00:13:05,263 --> 00:13:05,583
Hmm.

227
00:13:06,483 --> 00:13:06,843
Ah!

228
00:13:06,843 --> 00:13:12,543
Awaken now, dreamer!

229
00:13:12,663 --> 00:13:14,043
Dance like no one's looking!

230
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:17,383
It's okay to go a little bit crazy!

231
00:13:17,383 --> 00:13:19,143
Awaken now, dreamer!

232
00:13:19,143 --> 00:13:21,443
Let your heart feel desire excitement!

233
00:13:21,443 --> 00:13:24,903
Don't let the feeling ever die, die, die, die, die!

234
00:13:24,903 --> 00:13:26,943
Die, die, die, die, die, die!

235
00:13:26,943 --> 00:13:27,503
Hey guys!

236
00:13:27,663 --> 00:13:33,343
I understand that work can be super stressful, so we hope our performance helps you unwind and recover a little bit tonight!

237
00:13:33,343 --> 00:13:38,343
And there's nothing better than relaxing than Southern Chip Seed by Heatsanatha Farma Singles.

238
00:13:40,343 --> 00:13:51,343
I'm number one. That's number two, three, four, five, six, and zero. Together we're Froshu Shuu. Thanks for having us.

239
00:13:51,343 --> 00:13:53,343
And don't forget to keep on dreaming.

240
00:13:53,343 --> 00:14:08,343
Ah, never giving up. Awaken Returner, let your heart feel courage. Let's rise up and show the world how we can go, go, go, go. High, high, high, high.

241
00:14:08,343 --> 00:14:21,343
Awaken Returner, let your heart feel desire. A longing for miracles that can inspire. Awaken Returner, let your heart feel desire. Excitement, take joy wherever you can.

242
00:14:21,343 --> 00:14:23,343
Give it to me.

243
00:14:23,343 --> 00:14:29,343
Be for it and grab it. Don't back down. You've got it. To all the doubt you have said. Bye, bye, bye.

244
00:14:29,343 --> 00:14:36,343
Our passion, devotion, our deepest emotion. Our souls will be bare when we sing. Cut in.

245
00:14:36,343 --> 00:14:42,343
Songs for the soul and sorenship Z for the body. The perfect match.

246
00:14:51,343 --> 00:14:56,343
The crowd really liked us. I'm so happy.

247
00:14:56,343 --> 00:15:06,343
Sakura, don't take your makeup off. But it's bedtime. Not yet it isn't. Let's hit that hot spring.

248
00:15:06,343 --> 00:15:11,343
